@page "/circuit-check"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

@* Exists only to prove the Blazor Server circuit is live: a rendered page proves static SSR
   worked, but only a server round-trip after page load proves the circuit exists. Delete this
   page in S-01 (accounts-and-sessions) — by then real interactive surfaces exist, and S-01 is
   the slice that introduces an auth boundary this page would otherwise sit outside of.
   The @rendermode line above is the annotation every interactive page must carry: this app
   uses per-page opt-in, so a page without it renders statically and its handlers never fire. *@

<PageTitle>Circuit check</PageTitle>

<h1>Circuit check</h1>

<p>
    If the count below increases when you click, the SignalR circuit is live and the server is
    handling events for this page.
</p>

<p role="status">Current count: @currentCount</p>

<button class="btn btn-primary" @onclick="IncrementCount">Click me</button>

@code {
    private int currentCount = 0;

    private void IncrementCount()
    {
        currentCount++;
    }
}
